{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeLiftInterface","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Symmetric"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.tauRhoHodgeLift_of_loopWeightIsHodgeGram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.tauRhoHodgeLift_of_loopWeightIsHodgeGram","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HodgeGramLift.lean#L100-L110","doc":"**Wall-tightening theorem (conditional, sorry-free).** IF the loop weight is a\nHodge Gram (the single remaining open identification `LoopWeightIsHodgeGram`),\nTHEN `TauRhoHodgeLift` holds for it (with `Wbar = W`). The hypothesis is exactly\nthe open gap; the conclusion is the B2 lift. This is a genuine reduction — it does\nnot discharge the hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.LoopWeightIsHodgeGram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.LoopWeightIsHodgeGram","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HodgeGramLift.lean#L91-L98","doc":"**The single remaining identification, as a named `Prop` (OPEN).** The wall is\nnow exactly this: the categorical loop weight `W` on `H^{1,0}` equals the\ncomplexified Hodge Gram `Bᵀ·B` for some real mode data `B`. This file proves that\n*whenever* this holds, `TauRhoHodgeLift` is instantiated (via `hodgeGramLift`); it\ndoes NOT prove the identification itself. No instance/witness for the actual α_EM\nweight is provided — that is the open categorical input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.hodgeGramLift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.hodgeGramLift","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HodgeGramLift.lean#L82-L89","doc":"**The Hodge Gram instantiates `TauRhoHodgeLift`.** For any real `B` (the loop's\nmode data), the Hodge Gram `Bᵀ·B` — real symmetric, positive-semidefinite — gives\nan instance of the B2 lift class. This is the wall-tightening: the class is\ninhabited *by a Hodge Gram*. The remaining open identification is that the actual\nα_EM loop weight equals such a Gram — NOT proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.gram_isSymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.gram_isSymm","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HodgeGramLift.lean#L77-L80","doc":"A real **Gram** matrix `Bᵀ·B` is symmetric (`(Bᵀ·B)ᵀ = Bᵀ·B`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.hodgeSymmLift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.hodgeSymmLift","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HodgeGramLift.lean#L68-L75","doc":"**NON-CLOSING Hodge-side instance.** Given ANY real symmetric matrix `M` (a\nHodge datum on `H^{1,0}`), its complexification instantiates `TauRhoHodgeLift`\nwith `W = Wbar = complexify M`. Reduces the wall to \"loop weight = this `M`\" — it\ndoes NOT construct τ and does NOT prove the loop weight is of this form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.complexify_map_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.complexify_map_conj","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HodgeGramLift.lean#L59-L66","doc":"**Hodge reality.** A real matrix (complexified) is fixed by entrywise complex\nconjugation `ρ = starRingEnd ℂ`. This is the `conjugated` field with `Wbar = W`:\nthe `H^{0,1}` weight equals the (conjugate of the) `H^{1,0}` weight because the\nunderlying form is real. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.complexify_isHermitian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.complexify_isHermitian","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HodgeGramLift.lean#L50-L57","doc":"A real **symmetric** matrix, complexified, is Hermitian — the `hermitian`\nfield of `TauRhoHodgeLift`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.complexify","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HodgeGramLift.complexify","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HodgeGramLift.lean#L43-L48","doc":"**Complexification** of a real matrix: entrywise `Complex.ofReal`. Models the\n`H^{1,0} ⊕ H^{0,1}` embedding of a real Hodge datum into the complexified\ncohomology. ","signatureChunk":0}]}